Third-party components

FocusVM installs system tools and optional Python packages separately. The host
application distributions contain FocusVM source code and no third-party
executables or bundled dependencies. Qt for Python, libvirt, QEMU, virt-viewer,
Cage, and other optional tools retain their respective licenses and notices.

Fedora guest images are separate artifacts. Their installed packages retain
their respective licenses and notices, including the files under
/usr/share/licenses in the image. The guest builder records installed package
versions in packages.txt. A redistributed guest image also needs a review of
the applicable source and notice obligations and Fedora trademark terms.
